  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on the 27th October 2004 the matter described above is lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe proposed outbuilding that would be located more than 5m from the dwellinghouse as extended with a gabled roof with a ridge height of 3.6m above the existing ground level, which would not take the total area of outbuilding and extension coverage to more than 50% of the dwellings curtilage, constitutes permitted development as defined by Schedule 2, Part 1, Class E of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (as amended) and therefore does not require planning permission.\r\n\r\n\r\n"
